+# Feature Specification: JSON Pointer resolution
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) as `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`.
+**Standard**: RFC 6901 (JSON Pointer) §3 syntax, §4 evaluation, §5 JSON string representation. The URI fragment form (§6) is out of scope.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Read a value by pointer (Priority: P1)
+A service gives a JSON document and a pointer and gets back the referenced value.
+
+**Independent Test**: resolve every example of RFC 6901 §5 against its sample document.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. **Given** any document, **When** the pointer is `""`, **Then** the whole document is returned.
+2. **Given** `{"foo":["bar","baz"]}`, **When** pointer is `/foo/0`, **Then** `"bar"`.
+3. **Given** keys `a/b`, `m~n`, `""`, **When** pointers `/a~1b`, `/m~0n`, `/`, **Then** their values are returned (`~1` decoded before `~0`; `~01` means the key `~1`).
+4. **Given** a member whose value is `null`, **When** it is resolved, **Then** `null` is returned (not an error).
+
+### User Story 2 - Reject invalid or unresolvable pointers (Priority: P1)
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+1. A non-empty pointer not starting with `/` throws (§3).
+2. A `~` not followed by `0` or `1` throws (§3).
+3. A missing member, out-of-range index, or `-` (nonexistent element, §4) throws.
+4. Array indices with leading zeros, signs, or non-digits throw; descending into a primitive or `null` throws.
+5. Names such as `__proto__`, `constructor`, `toString` resolve only if they are own members of the object; inherited ones throw.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- The document and its contents are never mutated.
+- A non-string pointer is rejected with the same error type.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` is exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- **FR-002**: Pointer syntax follows RFC 6901 §3; violations throw `JsonPointerError`.
+- **FR-003**: Evaluation follows §4, including escape decoding and array index rules; failure to resolve throws `JsonPointerError`.
+- **FR-004**: Only own members are followed; inputs are not mutated.
+- **FR-005**: An existing member with value `null` is returned; a missing one throws.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- All RFC 6901 §5 examples pass; every invalid/unresolvable case above throws.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Documents are values as produced by JSON parsing. Members with duplicate names are not a concern.
